=== local-only
1. Never push to any remote and never open a PR. Work only on your `fm/tid` branch; juggernaut handles the merge into local `main`.
# Definition of done
Delivery contract: mode=local-only
Ship branch: fm/tid
This task ships **local-only**: no remote, no PR, no pipeline.
The task is complete only when committed on your branch `fm/tid`. Do NOT push, do NOT open a PR, do NOT merge.
A `done:` is accepted when the named head is on this project's shared local branch, not only on a detached copy; the check tests that head, not merely that a branch moved.
Keep your branch a clean fast-forward onto the current default branch - if `main` has advanced, rebase onto it so the eventual merge stays a fast-forward.
When it is implemented and committed, append `done [at=<epoch>]: ready in branch fm/tid` to the status file and stop.
The configured merge authority approves the ready branch, then juggernaut merges it into local `main` through the guarded fast-forward path.
Completion receipt: required
Before the final ready report (after validation in no-mistakes mode), write a nonempty evidence file containing commands run, results and limitations, then run `JG_HOME=/jg-home JG_RECEIPT_PR=<PR url> ROOT/core/receipts/bin/jg-run-receipt.sh tid PASS <evidence-file>` from the clean candidate checkout; a receipt for a PR needs JG_RECEIPT_PR.
Use FAIL when verification failed; never label failed or unperformed checks PASS.
The evidence file may be a task-owned temporary file outside your worktree; that write and the helper's completion-receipt write into its supervising state directory are authorized.
Regenerate the receipt after any candidate change, including validation fixes or a rebase.

QA: hand the feature to done-done and write no tests or proof by hand. At your final clean head, run `done-done affected`, then the repository's verify skill sealed with `done-done run -- <the suite command it names>`; done-done selects the journeys, runs them, judges them and seals the proof, so run no separate lint-and-tests pass of your own. Each of the nine steps has one owner: done-done owns intent, review, test, document and lint (a review question reaches your lead as the wait `lead`, reason `review`, and you never answer your own finding); the delivery style owns rebase, push, pull request and CI. If a journey your change touches has no coverage, extend that journey through done-done.
A `done:` naming a pull request needs that pull request's checks green: while a check is red or still running, the done is refused by the check's own name with the command to run it locally, so fix the cause or wait rather than report done.

A report that a user-visible change is fixed or done carries the released version that is running and where it is observable, or it says plainly that the change is merged but not released; `bin/jg-live-claim.sh` decides that from your report and the release record, and your lead or juggernaut applies it.
=== local-trunk
1. Never push, open a PR, merge, go live or release. Work only on your `fm/tid` branch; juggernaut lands it on the local trunk.
# Definition of done
Delivery contract: mode=local-trunk
Ship branch: fm/tid
This task ships **local-trunk**: one commit on the latest local trunk, no feature PR, no push, no release.
The commit message must carry this task id or its ticket key.
Run sealed done-done verification at your one commit's exact clean head. The landing check rebases it onto the trunk tip itself: a done lane waits as it is, and you never rebase it or report done again because the trunk moved.
Act only on a conflict the landing check names for your lane, or a red your own change caused: fix it in the lane, then report ready again.
Publish the completion receipt, then append `done [at=<epoch>]: ready in branch fm/tid (local-trunk)` and stop.
Juggernaut's existing trunk landing check lands that exact head and cleans up unforced.
Going live and releasing still require the captain's recorded word.
Completion receipt: required
Before the final ready report (after validation in no-mistakes mode), write a nonempty evidence file containing commands run, results and limitations, then run `JG_HOME=/jg-home JG_RECEIPT_PR=<PR url> ROOT/core/receipts/bin/jg-run-receipt.sh tid PASS <evidence-file>` from the clean candidate checkout; a receipt for a PR needs JG_RECEIPT_PR.
Use FAIL when verification failed; never label failed or unperformed checks PASS.
The evidence file may be a task-owned temporary file outside your worktree; that write and the helper's completion-receipt write into its supervising state directory are authorized.
Regenerate the receipt after any candidate change, including validation fixes or a rebase.

QA: hand the feature to done-done and write no tests or proof by hand. At your final clean head, run `done-done affected`, then the repository's verify skill sealed with `done-done run -- <the suite command it names>`; done-done selects the journeys, runs them, judges them and seals the proof, so run no separate lint-and-tests pass of your own. Each of the nine steps has one owner: done-done owns intent, review, test, document and lint (a review question reaches your lead as the wait `lead`, reason `review`, and you never answer your own finding); the delivery style owns rebase, push, pull request and CI. If a journey your change touches has no coverage, extend that journey through done-done.
A `done:` naming a pull request needs that pull request's checks green: while a check is red or still running, the done is refused by the check's own name with the command to run it locally, so fix the cause or wait rather than report done.

A report that a user-visible change is fixed or done carries the released version that is running and where it is observable, or it says plainly that the change is merged but not released; `bin/jg-live-claim.sh` decides that from your report and the release record, and your lead or juggernaut applies it.
=== no-mistakes on a base branch
1. Never push to the base branch `feat/x` or the default branch (push only your `fm/tid` branch). Never merge a PR.
=== direct-PR on gerrit
# Definition of done
Delivery contract: mode=direct-PR forge=gerrit shape=squash
Ship branch: fm/tid
This task ships **direct-PR** to a Gerrit review server: you publish the change yourself, after proving it with `done-done verify` (journeys, review and docs), and no pipeline run starts.
Gerrit has no pull requests, so there is nothing to open; publishing creates the change.
The task is complete only when committed on your branch.
When it is implemented and committed, publish it.
Publish from this copy with `gerrit-axi`, never with `git push`:
1. Run `git fetch origin` so the server's branch tip is in this repository; `gerrit-axi` reads its base off the server and refuses when that tip is not here.
2. Run `gerrit-axi publish --squash --json`, adding `--branch <b>` only when the task names a target branch other than the server's default.
   It is one push to `refs/for/<branch>` that turns every commit since your branch left the server's branch into ONE change carrying the oldest commit's message, so that message is the review description: make it the one you want reviewed.
   It keeps any `Change-Id` a commit already carries and stamps one into the oldest commit when it has none, rewriting your local branch's messages only.
   Never edit, remove, or regenerate a `Change-Id`: a different one creates a different change and orphans the first one's review, while the same one adds a patch set to it.
   Never pass `--stack`: a stack of changes is not published from this fleet until it can be watched by its membership pinned when its watch is armed, and the watch follows exactly one change.
3. Read the record it prints: `ok` must be `true`, and the one row of its `changes` table is your change. Its `url` is the change URL; when `url` is null, write `https://<host>/c/<project>/+/<change>` from your `origin` remote's host and that row's `project` and `change`.
   A failure prints a typed error record instead; fix what it names and publish again, which updates the same change rather than creating another.
Then append `done [at=<epoch>]: PR {change url} published for review` to the status file and stop. You are finished.
That `done:` is accepted only when the change's current patch set on the server carries this copy's HEAD tree, so commit nothing after publishing; if you must change the work, commit it and publish again before reporting done.
A `done:` whose URL is not the canonical `https://<host>/c/<project>/+/<number>` change URL is refused.
There is no pull request, no `gh-axi` call, and no forge CI result to report: a human reviewer approves and submits the change on the server, and juggernaut relays that outcome.
Completion receipt: required
Before the final ready report (after validation in no-mistakes mode), write a nonempty evidence file containing commands run, results and limitations, then run `JG_HOME=/jg-home JG_RECEIPT_PR=<PR url> ROOT/core/receipts/bin/jg-run-receipt.sh tid PASS <evidence-file>` from the clean candidate checkout; a receipt for a PR needs JG_RECEIPT_PR.
Use FAIL when verification failed; never label failed or unperformed checks PASS.
The evidence file may be a task-owned temporary file outside your worktree; that write and the helper's completion-receipt write into its supervising state directory are authorized.
Regenerate the receipt after any candidate change, including validation fixes or a rebase.

QA: hand the feature to done-done and write no tests or proof by hand. At your final clean head, run `done-done affected`, then the repository's verify skill sealed with `done-done run -- <the suite command it names>`; done-done selects the journeys, runs them, judges them and seals the proof, so run no separate lint-and-tests pass of your own. Each of the nine steps has one owner: done-done owns intent, review, test, document and lint (a review question reaches your lead as the wait `lead`, reason `review`, and you never answer your own finding); the delivery style owns rebase, push, pull request and CI. If a journey your change touches has no coverage, extend that journey through done-done.
A `done:` naming a pull request needs that pull request's checks green: while a check is red or still running, the done is refused by the check's own name with the command to run it locally, so fix the cause or wait rather than report done.

A report that a user-visible change is fixed or done carries the released version that is running and where it is observable, or it says plainly that the change is merged but not released; `bin/jg-live-claim.sh` decides that from your report and the release record, and your lead or juggernaut applies it.
